{
  "slug": "learned-behavior",
  "name": "Learned Behavior",
  "type": "plugin",
  "description": "Self-improving memory for Claude Code. Observes hooks (tool use, edits, errors, guard blocks), distills recurring patterns into durable rules, and surfaces relevant approved lessons before each task. No  LLM in the loop, no self-report, purely behavioral. Local SQLite, zero dependencies, no telemetry.",
  "longDescription": "Ships **3 commands** and **5 hooks**.\n\n- **Commands** (3): `advice` (Show relevant approved lessons for the current project), `mine` (Mine recent activity for new lesson candidates (errors, edit self-corrections, skill bypasses, guard blocks)), `review` (Review what's been learned in this project — lessons, candidates, and recurring errors)\n- **Hooks** (5): `SessionStart`, `UserPromptSubmit`, `PostToolUse`, `Stop`, `SessionEnd`\n\nInstalls with `claude plugin install learned-behavior@claude-community` from `lisn0/learned-behavior`.",
  "compatibility": [
    "claude"
  ],
  "pluginType": "package",
  "package": {
    "hook": 5,
    "command": 3
  },
  "sourceType": "community",
